menu "Cover art"

    config COVER_DECODE_TILE
        bool "Decode artwork into an RGB565 tile for a display"
        depends on SOC_JPEG_CODEC_SUPPORTED && SOC_PPA_SUPPORTED
        default y
        help
            On: every cover is decoded once (the JPEG engine, with stb_image for what it
            cannot read, and the PPA to scale) into a 280x280 RGB565 tile that a display draws
            and the web's GET /api/cover rebuilds a BMP from. What the P4 panel runs; it needs
            both engines, so a chip without them (the ESP32-S3) has only the mode below.

            Off: the cover is kept as the file that arrived, JPEG or PNG, and handed to the
            web as it is (cover_bytes_get); the browser decodes it. Its colour for the web's
            backdrop comes from an eighth-scale decode by the ROM's TJpgDec where the chip
            has one (baseline JPEG; none for PNG or progressive). For a board without a
            display: no tile memory, no software decoder, no seconds of CPU per cover.

endmenu
